{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "Vercel REST API \u2014 authored supplement",
    "version": "authored",
    "description": "Routes the vendored Vercel document never declared but the vendor's own emulator (vercel-labs/emulate, pinned in specs/vercel/emulate-inventory.json) serves: the /v1 API-key lifecycle, team creation and member listing, user patching, the registration probe, the v6 deployment listing, get-one env, and the local OAuth flow. Every cell is `authored` provenance \u2014 a reading of the oracle's packages/@emulators/vercel/src/routes/{api-keys,user,oauth,deployments,env}.ts, not of the real api.vercel.com. Two Edge Config listings are also here: the vendored document describes each as a single object under a sentence that says it lists, and the API answers an array, so the supplement states the array and the vendored operation of the same name yields to it."
  },
  "x-mirror-service": "vercel.api",
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://api.vercel.com"
    }
  ],
